---
import BlogLayout from '../../layouts/BlogLayout.astro';
import CopyButton from '../../components/CopyButton.astro';
import { authoredBlogMetadata, formatBlogDate } from '../../data/blogPresentation';
import { createBreadcrumbSchema, productFacts } from '../../data/productFacts';

const title = 'Parallel Git Worktrees With Zero Cloud Collisions';
const description = 'Work on a feature branch, PR review, and urgent hotfix simultaneously by isolating each Git worktree with its own LocalCloud Docker data volume.';
const pageUrl = new URL('blog/parallel-git-worktrees-localcloud/', productFacts.siteUrl).toString();
const metadata = authoredBlogMetadata['parallel-git-worktrees-localcloud'];
const contents = [
  { id: 'problem', label: 'Why shared cloud state breaks multitasking' },
  { id: 'solution', label: 'Pair Git worktrees with named data volumes' },
  { id: 'workflow', label: 'Run two isolated cloud stacks side by side' },
  { id: 'try-it', label: 'Try a branch-scoped runtime' },
  { id: 'cleanup', label: 'Tear down finished branch volumes cleanly' },
];
const worktreeCmd = `# Terminal 1: feature branch worktree
git worktree add ../repo-feature-search feat/search-index
cd ../repo-feature-search
localcloud start --local-only --data-volume feat-search
eval "$(localcloud env --data-volume feat-search)"

# Terminal 2: urgent hotfix worktree on its own volume and ports
git worktree add ../repo-hotfix fix/billing-export
cd ../repo-hotfix
localcloud start --local-only --data-volume hotfix-billing --accept-dynamic-ports
eval "$(localcloud env --data-volume hotfix-billing)"`;
const structuredData = [
  createBreadcrumbSchema([
    { name: 'Home', url: productFacts.siteUrl },
    { name: 'Blog', url: new URL('blog/', productFacts.siteUrl).toString() },
    { name: title, url: pageUrl },
  ]),
];
---

<BlogLayout {title} {description} {structuredData} {contents} article={{ publishedAt: metadata.publishedAt, headline: title }}>
  <Fragment slot="hero">
    <article class="site-section site-section--hero">
      <div class="container container--narrow">
        <nav class="mb-5 text-sm text-[var(--text-2)]" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/blog/">Blog</a></nav>
        <span class="site-eyebrow">Developer Productivity</span>
        <h1 class="mt-5">{title}</h1>
        <p class="blog-meta"><span>Published <time datetime={metadata.publishedAt}>{formatBlogDate(metadata.publishedAt)}</time></span><span>{metadata.minutes} min read</span><span>{metadata.topic}</span></p>
        <p class="blog-deck">Switching Git branches mid-feature—or running an AI agent on a second task—breaks when both checkouts mutate the same shared staging project. Give each worktree its own isolated LocalCloud volume.</p>
        <div class="blog-actions">
          <a class="site-button site-button--primary" href="/docs/configuration/#runtime-selection">Runtime selection guide</a>
          <a href="/docs/">Quick start</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </Fragment>

  <section class="site-section">
    <div class="container container--narrow space-y-10">
      <section>
        <h2 id="problem">Why shared cloud state breaks multitasking</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">Suppose you are halfway through testing a new BigQuery table schema on a feature branch when an urgent production hotfix lands—or you launch a coding agent in a second worktree to review a pull request.</p>
        <p class="mt-4">If both checkouts share one remote GCP dev environment or one database container, one branch’s migrations, Pub/Sub messages, and bucket deletions corrupt the other’s tests.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 id="solution">Pair Git worktrees with named data volumes</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">LocalCloud identifies each runtime by its Docker data volume via <code>--data-volume NAME</code> (defaulting to <code>localcloud-data</code>). Passing a branch-specific volume name starts a dedicated container with isolated storage, databases, and queues.</p>
        <ul class="site-list mt-5">
          <li><strong>Dynamic port allocation:</strong> When the default port range is already claimed by another branch’s runtime, pass <code>--accept-dynamic-ports</code> so the second instance binds free localhost ports automatically.</li>
          <li><strong>Shell-scoped routing:</strong> Running <code>eval "$(localcloud env --data-volume ...)"</code> injects that exact runtime’s ports into that terminal session alone.</li>
          <li><strong>Safe coexistence:</strong> LocalCloud tracks only containers it owns and never removes or relabels Docker resources belonging to another volume.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 id="workflow">Run two isolated cloud stacks side by side</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">Each terminal window runs its own Git worktree, its own test watcher, and its own local Google Cloud stack—with zero crosstalk between feature schemas and hotfix tests.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 id="try-it">Try a branch-scoped runtime</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">Spin up two parallel checkouts with independent LocalCloud volumes and environment exports. See <a href="/docs/configuration/#runtime-selection">Runtime selection</a> and <a href="/docs/">Getting Started</a> for installation and precedence rules.</p>
        <div class="site-panel mt-5">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4">
            <span class="site-kicker">Parallel worktree setup</span>
            <CopyButton text={worktreeCmd} analyticsLabel="copy-blog-worktree-cmd" />
          </div>
          <pre><code>{worktreeCmd}</code></pre>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 id="cleanup">Tear down finished branch volumes cleanly</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">When you merge a branch and remove its Git worktree, stop its container with <code>localcloud stop --data-volume hotfix-billing</code> and inspect <a href="/docs/configuration/#stop-reset-and-uninstall">stop and reset lifecycle docs</a> to remove unused Docker volumes cleanly.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</BlogLayout>
